# /etc/inittab - mpos: shells on the virtual consoles, kernel log on the serial line
#
# The one inittab both machines get. It is shared because everything below it
# is one kernel's answer on both machines since §13.16 ported the console
# multiplexer here: `tty1`..`tty4` are real pty-backed terminals everywhere,
# the vcmux carries each console's bytes over the serial wire on *both*, and
# `^A 1`..`^A 4` switches between them. A per-machine copy of this file used to
# be a fact about the second machine having no mux; that fact is gone, so the
# file is one.
#
# The respawn entries below name the virtual consoles `tty1`..`tty4`, and the
# serial port carries no getty of its own on either machine. Measured rather
# than assumed: because the vcmux carries the current console's bytes to the
# wire, a session whose guest was told `console=ttyAMA0` and nothing else - the
# windowless shape - still reaches `mpos login:` on the wire, and typing at it
# logs in on `tty1` (the current virtual console). A getty on the serial node
# was what this file used to render for that case, and it was a second login
# prompt next to the one busybox init already respawns.
#
# This file is the configuration - add a fifth console by adding a line, not by
# editing the build.

::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
tty2::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty2
tty3::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty3
tty4::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty4

# Stuff to do for the 3-finger salute
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Stuff to do before rebooting
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
